-- No database change needed here.
--
-- Notification.id had no default in schema.prisma, but every
-- prisma.notification.create() call in the codebase (admin/dashboard,
-- admin/publishing/books/[id] x2, bookstore/upload) creates a row
-- without supplying one -- each of those has been throwing at runtime.
--
-- The fix is schema.prisma now declaring id String @id @default(cuid()),
-- matching every other model. Prisma's cuid() default is generated by
-- Prisma Client itself before each insert (not a Postgres-level DEFAULT
-- clause -- compare how every other @default(cuid()) model's own
-- CREATE TABLE has no DEFAULT on its id column either), so there is no
-- column to alter. Running `npx prisma generate` after this migration
-- is what actually applies the fix.
--
-- This empty migration exists only so prisma migrate deploy's history
-- stays in sync with the schema.prisma change made alongside it.
SELECT 1;
